== Solution 2 ==

Since <imath>20\equiv2\pmod3</imath> and <imath>\text{Q}</imath> is in the 2nd diagonal, it is also in the 20th diagonal, and so we find that there are <imath>2(2 + 5 + 8 + 11 + 14 + 17) + 20 = 134 \text{Qs}</imath>. Since all the <imath>\text{P}</imath>'s and <imath>\text{R}</imath>'s are symmetric, the answer is <imath>\boxed{\textbf{(C)}~133\text{ Ps, }134\text{ Qs, }133\text{ Rs}}.</imath>

